{"availability":"available","full":"lyallcooper/justif","name":"justif","description":"Text justification for perfectionists","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":468,"forks":10,"created":"2026-07-15T03:41:25Z","updated":"2026-09-30T04:24:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://justif.lyall.co","topics":[],"demo":"https://justif.lyall.co/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:09.451Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:09.451Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:09.451Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:09.451Z","stars":468,"forks":10}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Justif is a JavaScript library that applies TeX-style paragraph layout to existing HTML, upgrading justified text on your website to print-quality. Justif chooses line breaks across the whole paragraph and uses hyphenation and microtypography techniques to produce more even spacing than the browser's built-in justification. It makes text easier and more enjoyable to read.","It is a progressive enhancement. Your HTML and CSS provide the initial and fallback rendering, while Justif upgrades paragraphs it can measure reliably. Unsupported paragraphs are left untouched. When JavaScript is disabled, native rendering is unchanged.","Browsers normally justify one line at a time. A locally acceptable break can make the next line too loose, create visible rivers of whitespace, or force a poor break near the end of the paragraph."],"features":["hyphenate words using bundled TeX patterns;","hang punctuation into the margin for a cleaner text edge;","make small per-line width adjustments on variable fonts with a wdth axis;","make small letter-spacing (tracking) adjustments when needed;","justify CJK text between characters with Japanese kinsoku rules."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lyallcooper/justif/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1c1ee7bd3d7273e82079e7a18876e2840bb943a9c7f2e20caedf239c98edbd56","extrac